<td style="width: 0"/><td style="width: 0.25in">(a)</td><td style="text-align: justify"><ix:footnote id="ix_1_footnote" xml:lang="en-US">Investments in subsidiaries are accounted for using the equity method in parent-only financial statements.
The carrying value is reduced to zero when the Company&#8217;s share of losses equals or exceeds its investment. Additional losses are
recognized as a liability and classified as &#8220;Excess losses over investment&#8221; if the Company has related financial obligations;
otherwise, they are not recognized. Subsequent profits are recognized only after prior unrecognized losses are recovered.</ix:footnote></td></tr></table></ix:nonNumeric></ix:nonNumeric><div>

